-- Diplomatic Appointments (Selection Process) Bill 2026 (Cth), first reading print (Senate),
-- 7 September 2026 (file 26S2721).
-- Part 3 -- Selection process for diplomatic appointments -- procedural provisions (ss 12-13).
--
-- Part 2 (ss 9-11) reads the Selection Committee this Part establishes, so this module comes
-- first in the import order: part2-selection.l4 imports it. The Selection Committee record is
-- declared here because s 12 creates the thing.

IMPORT `part1-preliminary`

§ `The Selection Committee and what it does`

-- One entry on the list of proposed candidates the Minister gives a Committee (s 10(1), (2)).
-- s 10(2)(d) requires reasons for each candidate with a significant political affiliation; the
-- entry records whether the list sets them out.
DECLARE `list entry` HAS
    `candidate`                                       IS A Person
    `the list sets out reasons despite the affiliation` IS A BOOLEAN

-- What the Committee's written notice under s 10(3) does: recommend a named candidate
-- (s 10(3)(a)) or refer the matter back to the Minister (s 10(3)(b)).
DECLARE `notice content` IS ONE OF
    `recommending` HAS `the candidate's name` IS A STRING
    `referring the matter back to the Minister`

-- A Selection Committee, with everything ss 10, 12 and 13 ask of it. Day numbers throughout.
-- The decision recorded is the one the notice reports: the votes are the votes on that
-- question at the meeting.
DECLARE `Selection Committee` HAS
    `established on`                                   IS A NUMBER
    `established by written instrument`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `members appointed`                                IS A NUMBER
    `members appointed by written instrument`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the members have an appropriate balance under s 12(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `list given`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `list given on`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `list`                                             IS A LIST OF `list entry`
    `decision made at a meeting`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `members present at the meeting`                   IS A NUMBER
    `votes for`                                        IS A NUMBER
    `votes against`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `notice given`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `notice given on`                                  IS A NUMBER
    `notice`                                           IS A `notice content`

§ `12 Minister may establish Selection Committees`

-- s 12(1): "The Minister may, by written instrument, establish a committee for the purpose of
-- recommending an appointment to a designated diplomatic office."
-- s 12(2): "Each such committee is to be known as the Selection Committee for the appointment to
-- the designated diplomatic office."
-- s 10(5): "The Selection Committee is dissolved after giving the Minister written notice as
-- required by subsection (3)." A Committee exists from the day it is established until the day
-- it gives its notice; on the day of the notice it is dissolved, and another may be established
-- that day (ENCODING-NOTES.md, E-14).
@ref s 12(1), (2); s 10(5)
GIVEN c IS A `Selection Committee`, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Committee` c `is in existence on` d IF
        c's `established on` AT MOST d
    AND (NOT (c's `notice given` AND c's `notice given on` AT MOST d))

-- s 10(5): dissolution.
@ref s 10(5)
GIVEN c IS A `Selection Committee`, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Committee` c `is dissolved by` d IF
    c's `notice given` AND c's `notice given on` AT MOST d

-- A Committee established before day d that is still in existence on d.
GIVEN cs IS A LIST OF `Selection Committee`
      d  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a Committee established earlier in` cs `is in existence on` d MEANS
    CONSIDER cs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN c FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        (c's `established on` LESS THAN d AND `the Committee` c `is in existence on` d)
     OR `a Committee established earlier in` rest `is in existence on` d

-- s 12(8): "No more than one Selection Committee for an appointment to a designated diplomatic
-- office may be established at any one time (despite subsection (1))."
-- The Minister may establish a Committee on day d for an appointment if no Committee for it
-- established earlier is then in existence. `others` are the Committees for that appointment
-- (the list may include the new one: only those established before d are read). Two Committees
-- established on the same day are not caught (ENCODING-NOTES.md, E-14).
@ref s 12(1), (8)
GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, others IS A LIST OF `Selection Committee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 12(8) allows a Committee to be established on` d `beside` others IF
    (NOT `a Committee established earlier in` others `is in existence on` d)

-- s 12(1) and (8): whether a Committee was established in accordance with s 12, given the other
-- Committees for the same appointment established before it.
@ref s 12(1), (8)
GIVEN c IS A `Selection Committee`, others IS A LIST OF `Selection Committee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Committee` c `was established in accordance with s 12, beside` others IF
        c's `established by written instrument`
    AND `section 12(8) allows a Committee to be established on` (c's `established on`) `beside` others

-- s 12(3): "A Selection Committee is to consist of 3 members."
-- s 12(4): "The members of a Selection Committee are to be appointed by the Minister by written
-- instrument."
-- s 12(5): "In appointing a person as a member of a Selection Committee, the Minister must ensure
-- that the Selection Committee's members collectively have an appropriate balance of expertise,
-- qualifications, skills or experience in the following: (a) diplomacy; (b) foreign policy;
-- (c) international affairs; (d) international relations; (e) international trade; (f) public
-- administration." Whether the balance is appropriate is the Minister's judgment, taken as a fact.
@ref s 12(3), (4), (5)
GIVEN c IS A `Selection Committee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Committee's membership complies with s 12(3) to (5)` c IF
        c's `members appointed` EQUALS 3
    AND c's `members appointed by written instrument`
    AND c's `the members have an appropriate balance under s 12(5)`

-- s 12(6): "The rules may make provision for or in relation to Selection Committees, including ...
-- (a) procedures ...; (b) meetings ... (subject to section 13); (c) dissolution ... (subject to
-- subsection 10(5)); (d) terms and conditions of appointment of members; (e) remuneration of
-- members; (f) disclosure of interests by members; (g) resignation of members; (h) termination
-- of appointment of members." No rules have been made (REF-06); nothing to decide.
-- s 12(7): "An instrument made under subsection (1) or (4) is not a legislative instrument."
-- Declaratory (REF-28); nothing to decide.

§ `13 Meetings of Selection Committees`

-- s 13(2): "At a meeting of a Selection Committee, a quorum is constituted by all 3 members."
@ref s 13(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Selection Committee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the meeting was quorate` c IF
    c's `members present at the meeting` AT LEAST 3

-- s 13(3): "A question arising at a meeting of the Selection Committee is to be determined by a
-- majority of the votes of the members."
-- FORK-07, reading A (taken): a majority of the votes of the members is more than half of the
-- members' votes, so at least 2 of the 3 members must vote for the question (EM para 23 and 33
-- read it so).
@ref s 13(3)
GIVEN c IS A `Selection Committee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the question was carried` c IF
    (c's `votes for` TIMES 2) GREATER THAN 3

-- FORK-07, reading B: a majority of the votes cast, so abstentions do not count.
@ref s 13(3)
GIVEN c IS A `Selection Committee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the question was carried, reading B` c IF
    c's `votes for` GREATER THAN c's `votes against`

-- s 13(1): "A decision of a Selection Committee under subsection 10(3) must be made at a meeting
-- of the Selection Committee." Read with s 13(2): at a quorate meeting.
@ref s 13(1), (2)
GIVEN c IS A `Selection Committee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision was made at a quorate meeting` c IF
    c's `decision made at a meeting` AND `the meeting was quorate` c
